<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al-Julanda ibn Mas'ud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 752</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Julanda ibn Mas'ud was the first Ibadi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a>, elected around 750 by the Ibadi scholars and leaders after the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a>. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imamate">imamate</a> was short: in 752 an army sent by the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> defeated and killed him, ending the first Ibadi state in Oman. Ibadi tradition remembers him as a model of the just imam who died in defence of the community.</p></div>
